<title>USA: GE division says gets Lauda Air contract.</title>
<headline>GE division says gets Lauda Air contract.</headline>
<dateline>EVANDALE, Ohio 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>GE Engine Services Inc, a division of General Electric Co , said Friday it had been given a ten-year contract worth about $50 million from Lauda Air of Austria.</p>
<p>The company said its maintenance cost per hour contract covers maintenance, repair, and overhaul of GE90 engines powering Lauda's four Boeing 777-200 aircraft.</p>
<p>The company said delivery of the first 777 to Lauda Air is scheduled for September 1997, with the remaining three aircraft to be delivered by the year 2001.</p>
